  "vendor_website": "danfoss.com",
  "description": "AC drives with built-in Modbus RTU and Modbus TCP: control and status words, speed reference and actual speed, process data out (frequency, speed, current, torque, power, voltages, fault), counters, energy, fault history and timeout",
  "revision": 1,
  "source": "Danfoss, VACON 100 family Modbus RTU and Modbus TCP user manual (BC361182856709en-000401)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "VACON 100 Modbus RTU & Modbus TCP – User manual",
      "version": "BC361182856709en-000401",
      "url": "https://assets.danfoss.com/documents/270144/BC361182856709en-000401.pdf",
      "note": "chapter 6.3 (data mapping) and appendices 1-2",
      "accessed": "2026-11-15",
      "sha256": "b2d54f0cd4e32242ae82504511f1f98c6d202bc7ce6df066b1def0da625b40e7"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU and Modbus TCP. Functions 01-06, 15, 16 and 23. Addresses are those of the manual, counted from 1: the manual's frame example writes register 2001 at address 2000 (address_base 1).",
    "Holding and input registers hold the same values (input register 1 is holding 40001, and so on).",
    "32-bit process data and counters are high word first (2051/2052 for the control word, 40011/40012 for the day counter).",
    "Process data out 1-8 hold the default IDs listed here; the application can map other values to them. Application parameters are read by their ID: 16-bit at address = ID (1-2000, 2200-10000), 32-bit at 20000 + ID; the ID map (10501-10530 with data at 10601 on) packs chosen IDs together.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "tcp+rtu",
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 1,
  "x_status": "official",
